experiment.prespecified:
Fixed 2026-11-19, before any zoo result was read (borg-reborn-rs#584, PR #612). Pilot (RULES 16); small and
larger only after this gate and the owner.
Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's two #584 values in borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified and key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced;
- in ctl, no "# Phase (<site>): no, no enemy on an adjacent square", "... fight is not lost" or "... phase allowed" note.
Report per arm and per class, from every game's messages:
- deaths and causes, final level, deepest level;
- paired rescued and newly killed against ctl;
- Phase Doors done ("# Phase (<site>): done"), per site; the rule's notes per game (no adjacent enemy, fight not lost,
  phase allowed) and its boosts ("# Phase (<site>) boost: <what>");
- deaths with no Phase Door left (no Phase Door in the pack at death) and deaths within 200 game turns of a refused phase.
Context: a local run on the same tree (harness binary, BORG_CORE=borg-rs, the 18 classes-18 starts, 100,000 turns; not
a zoo run): ctl 150 Phase Doors and 0 deaths; rule at 100: 83 Phase Doors, 18 boosts, 1 death (Rogue 1502695781, wild
cat on DL1, no Phase Door left). 18 starts per arm show direction only.
